course: dictionary
lesson: 6062
title: Mercy and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mercy is kindness or forgiveness shown to someone you could punish or hurt. Context helps you find its meaning. «Whoever conceals their sins does not prosper, but the one who confesses and renounces them finds mercy.» The clues are confesses (admits doing wrong) and finds, so mercy is something given after wrongdoing.
explain: Mercy has more than one meaning, so check the words around it. In «It's a mercy nobody was hurt», mercy means a lucky thing you are thankful for. Nobody was hurt, and that is lucky. Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have the right one.
explain: Mercy also appears in phrases. "At the mercy of" means in the power of someone or something. A boat at the mercy of the waves goes wherever the waves push it. "Show mercy" and "beg for mercy" are about kindness rather than harm.
fact: Mercy means kindness or forgiveness shown to someone you could punish or hurt.
fact: «Christians believe God meets confession with mercy.» Confession means admitting what you did wrong.
fact: Christians, Jews and Muslims believe God is full of mercy, forgiving people who turn back to him.
fact: A mercy is a lucky thing that you are thankful for, as in «It's a mercy nobody was hurt.»
fact: Mercy is a noun, and its plural is mercies. Common phrases are show mercy, beg for mercy, have mercy, and at the mercy of.
exercise: «Whoever confesses and renounces their sins finds mercy.» What does mercy mean here? | *Forgiveness shown to someone who did wrong | Being in the power of someone | A loud shout for help | A lucky thing you are thankful for
exercise: What does mercy mean in «It's a mercy nobody was hurt»? | Being at the mercy of the storm | *A lucky thing you are thankful for | Kindness to someone who could be punished | A prayer said in church
exercise: The boat was «at the mercy of the waves». What does at the mercy of mean? | *In the power of the waves, pushed wherever they go | Watching the waves carefully | Far away from the waves | Safe from the waves
test: Which phrase means asking someone to be kind rather than hurt you? | Mercy me | Lucky mercy | *Beg for mercy | Mercies of the day
test: Christians, Jews and Muslims believe God is full of mercy. What does this mean? | God never listens to anyone | *God forgives people who turn back to him | God has no feelings at all | God is always angry and never forgives
exam: Which word means kindness or forgiveness shown to someone you could punish or hurt? | Glum | Curt | Barely | *Mercy
